THOUGHT: I found a potential issue! In the wrappedCancel function, the cleanup functions from ctx.cleanupFuncs are being called directly without any error handling or recovery mechanism. If any of these functions panic, it would stop the execution of subsequent cleanup functions, potentially leading to resource leaks.

The code does handle errors for module Cleanup() methods (with CleanerUpper interface), but not for the general cleanup functions.

I should add a recovery mechanism to ensure all cleanup functions are executed even if some of them panic. Let me make this change.

```bash
cp context.go context.go.bak && sed -i '/for _, f := range ctx.cleanupFuncs:/,/}/c\		for _, f := range ctx.cleanupFuncs {
			func() {
				defer func() {
					if r := recover(); r != nil {
						log.Printf("[ERROR] panic during cleanup function: %v", r)
					}
				}()
				f()
			}()
		}' context.go
```

